    title_en: "Japan Food Giant Nichirei Hacked, Halting Cold Chain Logistics and Threatening Food Shortages in the Restaurant Industry",
    summary_en: "Nichirei Group, a major Japanese food and low-temperature logistics provider, was hit by a cyberattack on July 13th, causing a complete shutdown of its refrigerated warehouses and frozen food dispatch operations. The incident was confirmed to be due to unauthorized external access, directly impacting Nichirei Group's inbound and outbound logistics, as well as Nichirei Foods' frozen food supply chain. Given that Nichirei is a critical hub for Japan's cold chain logistics, the resulting ripple effects have impacted multiple restaurant and retail businesses, including KFC, Kura Sushi, and Aeon. These affected businesses are facing the crisis of ingredient shortages and have even been forced to temporarily suspend operations. This incident highlights the extreme vulnerability of critical infrastructure (such as the food supply chain) to cyberattacks, reminding companies that they must strengthen the cybersecurity resilience and backup mechanisms of their supply chains.",
