    title: "Imagination PowerVR BXM-4-64 GPU 韌體正式上游化，支援阿里巴巴 T-Head TH1520 平台",
    summary: "本篇報導指出，Imagination Technologies 的 PowerVR BXM-4-64 GPU 韌體已正式被納入 `linux-firmware.git` 的上游儲存庫。此舉為利用開源 GPU 驅動堆疊（包括 PowerVR DRM 核心驅動和 Mesa 中的 PowerVR Vulkan 驅動）提供了關鍵的缺失環節。該 GPU 結合了阿里巴巴開發的 T-Head TH1520 SoC，這款晶片採用四核心 RISC-V CPU（Xuantie C910）設計。目前支援的應用設備包括 Lichee Pi4A 和 BeagleV Ahead 等開發板。韌體上游化讓開發者能更順暢地在 Linux 環境下使用此開源 GPU 驅動，提升了整體使用者體驗。此更新對於 RISC-V 生態系和開源硬體加速的開發者群體具有實質意義。",
    tags: ["Imagination PowerVR", "BXM-4-64", "linux-firmware.git", "RISC-V", "T-Head TH1520", "Mesa", "Linux 核心"],
    title_en: "Imagination PowerVR BXM-4-64 GPU Firmware Officially Upstreamed, Supporting Alibaba T-Head TH1520 Platform",
    summary_en: "This report indicates that Imagination Technologies' PowerVR BXM-4-64 GPU firmware has been officially incorporated into the upstream repository `linux-firmware.git`. This move provides a critical missing link for utilizing the open-source GPU driver stack (including the PowerVR DRM kernel driver and the PowerVR Vulkan driver in Mesa). The GPU is combined with the T-Head TH1520 SoC, developed by Alibaba, which features a quad-core RISC-V CPU (Xuantie C910). Currently supported application devices include the Lichee Pi4A and BeagleV Ahead development boards. The firmware upstreaming allows developers to use this open-source GPU driver more smoothly in a Linux environment, enhancing the overall user experience. This update holds significant importance for developers in the RISC-V ecosystem and open-source hardware acceleration.",
