    id: "20260716-018",
    trackers: ["eu_cra"],
    category: "法令更新",
    title: "歐盟委員會接受 X 平台修復計畫，要求提升透明度並開放研究資料以符合《數位服務法案》",
    summary: "歐盟委員會已接受 X 平台為符合《數位服務法案》（DSA）的行動計畫。此舉是繼委員會於 2025 年 12 月裁定 X 違反 DSA 並處以罰款之後。修復措施要求 X 改善其廣告儲存庫，提供更佳的搜尋功能和更快的響應時間，並透過 API 公布更多廣告資訊。此外，X 必須改善研究人員的資料存取流程，確保有資格的研究人員能免費取得公共資料，並更新服務條款，不得以合約方式禁止研究人員爬取公共資料。X 需在六個月內實施這些措施，並提交獨立外部稽核報告給委員會。委員會將密切監控進度，特別關注數位服務委員會（Board for Digital Services）提出的意見，確保 X 的行動計畫能充分解決所有違規問題。",
    tags: ["歐盟委員會", "Digital Services Act", "DSA", "X 平台", "透明度義務", "研究資料存取"],
    title_en: "European Commission Accepts X Platform Remediation Plan, Mandating Increased Transparency and Open Research Data to Comply with Digital Services Act",
    summary_en: "The European Commission has accepted X Platform's action plan to comply with the Digital Services Act (DSA). This follows the Commission's December 2025 ruling that X violated the DSA and imposed a fine. The remediation measures require X to improve its advertising repository, provide better search functionality and faster response times, and disclose more advertising information via API. Furthermore, X must improve the data access process for researchers, ensuring that qualified researchers can freely access public data, and update its terms of service so that contractual agreements cannot prohibit researchers from scraping public data. X must implement these measures within six months and submit an independent external audit report to the Commission. The Commission will closely monitor progress, paying particular attention to the opinions issued by the Board for Digital Services, to ensure X's action plan fully resolves all non-compliance issues.",
    tags_en: ["European Commission", "Digital Services Act", "DSA", "X Platform", "Transparency Obligation", "Research Data Access"],
    sources: [
      { name: "EC CRA 實施頁面", url: "https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/news/commission-accepts-xs-action-plan-comply-digital-services-act", lang: "EN" }
    ]
