    category: "Apple",
    title: "深入探討 App Store 紀錄用戶點擊行為：Apple 平台隱私與安全機制分析",
    summary: "本文內容來自 Mysk 的 Security Bite 播客，討論了 Apple 平台在應用程式商店（App Store）的數據紀錄機制。核心議題是 App Store 如何記錄用戶每一次的點擊（tap）行為，這對於用戶的隱私和數據安全構成關注點。內容指出，Apple 的系統機制會記錄這些操作，這讓研究人員對用戶數據的收集範圍和深度產生了疑問。此外，文章也提及了研究人員正在公開地從 Apple 的漏洞賞金計畫（bug bounty program）中退出，暗示了對 Apple 安全政策或透明度的不滿。為了解決這些問題，Mysk 推出了名為 Loupe 的免費開源應用程式，該工具旨在展示 iOS API 實際分享了哪些關於用戶的資訊，幫助用戶了解數據流向。實務上，用戶應提高警覺，了解其在 Apple 生態系統中的操作數據被記錄的範圍，並利用開源工具進行自我審核。",
    tags: ["Apple", "iOS", "App Store", "數據隱私", "漏洞賞金", "Mysk", "Loupe"],
    title_en: "In-Depth Analysis of App Store Recording of User Click Behavior: Apple Platform Privacy and Security Mechanism Analysis",
    summary_en: "This article content is derived from Mysk's Security Bite podcast, discussing the data logging mechanisms on the Apple platform within the App Store. The core issue is how the App Store records every user tap, which raises concerns regarding user privacy and data security. The content points out that Apple's system mechanisms record these operations, leading researchers to question the scope and depth of user data collection. Furthermore, the article mentions researchers publicly withdrawing from Apple's bug bounty program, suggesting dissatisfaction with Apple's security policies or transparency. To address these issues, Mysk released a free open-source application called Loupe. This tool aims to demonstrate what information the iOS API actually shares about the user, helping users understand data flow. Practically, users should raise awareness regarding the scope of operational data recorded within the Apple ecosystem and utilize open-source tools for self-auditing.",
    tags_en: ["Apple", "iOS", "App Store", "Data Privacy", "Bug Bounty", "Mysk", "Loupe"],
    sources: [
      { name: "9to5Mac", url: "https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/16/security-bite-podcast-apple-is-watching-your-taps", lang: "EN" }
    ]
