    title_en: "Google Health Service Experiences Major Outage, Affecting Data Sync for All Fitbit and Pixel Watch Devices",
    summary_en: "On July 15, the Google Health service experienced a major outage, preventing all users utilizing Google Health from syncing device data. The issue persisted for approximately 7 hours, affecting devices such as Fitbit and Pixel Watch. Users reported that even when activity data (such as step counts) was recorded on the watch, syncing to the Google Health application resulted in errors or data failure to load, displaying error code 1001. Although Google has not disclosed the cause of the failure, an official statement indicated that due to the existence of local storage mechanisms, users' actual data should be retained. Once the sync function is restored, Google Health should be able to pull the data recorded during the period of disruption. Furthermore, the Health Coach's questioning and summarization features were also impacted by this outage. Google has since fixed the issue, but still advises users that there is no absolute guarantee regarding the completeness of data backfilling.",
