    summary_en: "YouTube Music is testing a new interface design: full-screen cover art. Currently, cover art typically appears between the audio/video switcher and the song title, featuring rounded corners. The new design will allow the cover art to occupy the entire screen, even including the status and system navigation bars. This change transforms the interface from square to rectangular, which may result in some content being cropped. This design change also applies to viewing music videos, reflecting the current popular trend of 'short-form' vertical video. Furthermore, in the operation carousel area, button backgrounds will become transparent, and YouTube Music has completely abandoned the color-themed design based on cover art. This design is currently in the testing phase and has not been fully rolled out. This update primarily affects the user interface experience of YouTube Music, rather than core functionality or security vulnerabilities.",
