    title_en: "Google AI Mode expands integration with YouTube Music, Canva, and Instacart, enhancing cross-application contextual experiences",
    summary_en: "Google's AI Mode is continuously expanding its cross-application integration capabilities, making its functions more closely aligned with users' daily work and life scenarios. Initially supporting linked applications like Gmail and Google Photos, it later added Google Drive and Calendar, allowing it to automatically plan itineraries based on the user's calendar and directly add events. This update focuses on integrating YouTube Music, allowing users to generate playlists based on their needs through AI Mode and operate directly within the results interface. Furthermore, AI Mode has expanded to Canva and Instacart, enabling users to directly search for design templates using Canva or add ingredients directly to the Instacart shopping cart when planning a grocery list, achieving a smoother cross-platform operation. This feature is currently rolling out in the US region, and Google has announced that it will continue to add more partners in the future, expanding the ecosystem breadth of AI Mode.",
