    summary_en: "Google announced that its research tool, NotebookLM, will be renamed Gemini Notebook, closely linking its brand with the core Gemini brand. The product is positioned as the \"premier research tool\" and will be increasingly integrated into the Google ecosystem. This includes use within the Gemini application for chat organization, and future integration into Google Search's AI mode. Furthermore, Google announced upgraded features for Gemini 3.5 and Antigravity. These features, originally launched for AI Ultra users, will now be expanded to all AI Pro subscribers. This upgrade aims to provide a secure cloud computing environment for each notebook, enabling native code writing and execution, thereby serving \"complex data analysis based on user data.\" Google emphasized that this update will provide new output formats and deeper analytical capabilities. Currently, Gemini Notebook is used by over thirty million users and six hundred thousand organizations.",
