    summary_en: "According to reports, Apple's next-generation Apple Silicon chip, the M6, is expected to launch later this year. Compared to the current M5, the M6 will significantly increase memory bandwidth, boosting it from the current 153 GB/s to 200 GB/s, which will significantly improve on-device AI performance. Furthermore, the M6 will feature a redesigned GPU, with the core count expected to increase from 10 cores in the M5 to 12 cores, helping to enhance performance for gaming, video rendering, and GPU-accelerated applications. However, the launch of the M6 is rumored to change Apple's traditional product line strategy, with reports suggesting Apple may only release a base model and no longer offer high-end versions like Pro, Max, or Ultra. The next more advanced M7 chip is anticipated to launch in the first half of 2027 and is expected to feature even higher memory bandwidth. The M6 has currently been tested in updated base model MacBook Pros, but its application to other products remains to be seen.",
