    title_en: "Roblox announces 'Game Creation' feature debut on mobile, supporting cross-platform creation for iPhone/iPad/Android",
    summary_en: "The gaming platform Roblox is set to launch the revolutionary 'Roblox Build' feature, bringing game creation capabilities to mobile applications for the first time. This feature allows users to quickly generate playable new game experiences directly within the iPhone and iPad apps using text prompts powered by AI. Roblox emphasizes that Build aims to extend the existing desktop creation tool, Roblox Studio, to mobile devices. This update not only removes the limitation of game creation being restricted to Mac or PC but also allows creators to start working in Build, utilizing shared backends, models, and chat history. Furthermore, creators can enhance their work using Studio's broader capabilities or monitor the progress of agents dispatched from Studio on the mobile device. Roblox Build will launch in Alpha testing starting July 28th, beginning in New Zealand, supporting the three major platforms: iPhone, iPad, and Android, significantly lowering the barrier to game development.",
