    summary_en: "This report compares existing blood pressure monitoring devices. The Apple Watch (including Series 11, Series 10, Series 9, Ultra 3, Ultra 2), supported by watchOS 26, can measure blood pressure and issue potential high blood pressure alerts, but cannot provide actual blood pressure numerical values. Other similar devices also primarily utilize this type of alert mechanism. However, the Signal Ring, launched by the startup Vital Signals, claims to provide complete blood pressure measurement data with accuracy comparable to traditional arm cuffs, without requiring any calibration. The device is expected to be delivered in October and is priced at $399. Although devices like the Oura Ring have undergone clinical trials, Signal Ring's claims are highly controversial, especially given its professional focus on high-risk elderly populations. Consumers needing blood pressure monitoring should pay attention to the device's accuracy and medical certification.",
