    summary_en: "OnePlus has officially announced that, as part of its global strategy adjustment, it will cease launching new mobile phone products in North America and Europe. This move signals a significant reduction in the brand's global market coverage. Previously, OnePlus expanded its presence in the US market through collaborations with carriers like T-Mobile and Verizon, and had launched flagship models such as the OnePlus 15. However, the new strategy indicates that future new product launches will primarily focus on the Indian and Chinese markets. For existing users, OnePlus will continue to provide software support, but their devices will transition from the original OxygenOS system to Oppo's ColorOS, and will be upgraded to Android 17. This represents the brand deeply integrating its software ecosystem and product line planning with its parent company, Oppo, and adjusting its core market focus.",
