    summary_en: "AMD has officially announced ROCm 7.14 as the new production version, replacing the previously technical preview 7.9+ series. This version marks a new foundation for the AMD AI software platform and utilizes TheRock for its production build and release infrastructure. Key updates in ROCm 7.14 include official support for the Ryzen AI 400 series chips, covering products such as Ryzen AI Max+ PRO 495/490/485, as well as the lower-end Ryzen AI 430/440 series. Furthermore, it adds official support for the Instinct MI350P hardware across RHEL 9.8, RHEL 10.2, SUSE Linux Enterprise 15 SP7/SLES 16, and Debian 13. On the technical front, ROCm 7.14 enhances GPU virtualization, AI inference capabilities, and framework enhancements, while also incorporating multiple HIP enhancements to improve compatibility with CUDA. AMD advises users on 7.2 or older versions to follow official documentation for migration. Developers should leverage the tools, performance, and flexibility provided by this version to build next-generation AI applications.",
